# Contributing to HEC-FDA

Thank you for contributing to HEC-FDA. Any contribution you submit is subject to the license of this project, found in the [LICENSE](LICENSE) file. Code should follow Microsoft's [C# coding conventions](https://learn.microsoft.com/dotnet/csharp/fundamentals/coding-style/coding-conventions) and [.NET framework design guidelines](https://learn.microsoft.com/dotnet/standard/design-guidelines/). Whenever possible, follow the patterns already established in the codebase; where a new feature needs to deviate from them, document that deviation explicitly in the code and in the pull request. Note that the GitHub repository is a read-only mirror. Contributors should work with HEC to make pull requests against the canonical repository, while GitHub Issues remain open for bug reports and feature requests.
